# Browser-check output — regenerated by `npm run e2e`, never reviewed as source.
#
# The visual baselines are per platform: Playwright renders them with the platform's own fonts, so
# a set generated on Windows fails on Linux for reasons that have nothing to do with the code.
#
# Only CI's set is committed, because CI is the one machine whose rendering is fixed. A baseline
# that is not committed is written fresh on every CI run and therefore passes every time, which
# looks like a visual check and is not one. A developer's own platform writes its set on the first
# local run and keeps it there.
e2e/screens.spec.ts-snapshots/*-win32.png
e2e/screens.spec.ts-snapshots/*-darwin.png
e2e/screenshots/
test-results/
playwright-report/
